00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:30.276 line:92%
Tell everyone what it's about.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:32.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you haven't seen season one
get ready to binge.

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. So, if you haven't see
season one,

00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:37.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mindhunter" is basically
the origin story

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Behavioral Science Unit
in the FBI.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:43.990
It's about the team that came up
with the term "serial killer."

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
This idea of going into jail
and interviewing

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:50.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
incarcerated mass murderer
to glean information

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
to then prevent crimes
from happening.

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then, we think of that ide
in the first season,

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:59.772
and in the second season, we try
to make it work on the field

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
We interview
more serial killers.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
We get involved
in the Atlanta child murders

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was a famous case
in the early '80s,

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:09.315
and continue the sort of
psychological exploration

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:09.949 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of serial killers.

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:12.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
